hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27661","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ishaq, he said: Haddathana Ibn Lahi'ah, he said: Haddathana Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from al-Harith ibn Ya'qub, from Ya'qub ibn al-Ashajj, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, from Khawlah, she said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever alights in a place and says: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created, nothing shall harm him until he departs from it."
"27662","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ishaq, he said: Haddathana Ibn Lahi'ah, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, from Ya'qub ibn al-Ashajj, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, from Khawlah, she said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying like that."
"27663","Haddathana Hajjaj, he said: Akhbarana Layth, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me from al-Harith, from Ya'qub ibn Abd Allah, he narrated to him that he heard Busr ibn Sa'id saying: I heard Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas saying: I heard Khawlah bint Hakim al-Sulamiyyah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever alights in a place then says: I seek refuge in all the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created, nothing shall harm him until he departs from that place of his."
"27664","Haddathana Abu Mu'awiyah, he said: Haddathana Hajjaj, from al-Rabi' ibn Malik, from Khawlah bint Hakim, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever alights in a place and says: I seek refuge in all the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created, nothing in that place of his shall harm him until he departs from it."
"27853","Affan narrated to us: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Ya'qub ibn Abdillah ibn al-Ashajj, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Sa'd, from Khawlah bint Hakim, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If one of you, when he stops at a dwelling, says: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created, nothing in that dwelling will harm him until he departs from it."
"27854","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Hajjaj, and Yazid ibn Harun, he said: al-Hajjaj informed us, from al-Rabi' ibn Malik, he said: Khawlah bint Hakim said. Muhammad ibn Yazid said: The wife of Uthman ibn Maz'un. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no Muslim who stops at a dwelling and says when he stops: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created, and Yazid said: Three times, except he is protected from the evil of that dwelling of his until he departs from it."
"27855","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Khawlah bint Hakim, that she asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. He said: There is no washing upon her until fluid is emitted, just as there is no washing upon a man until he emits."
"27856","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj, he said: Shu'bah narrated to me, he said: I heard Ata' al-Khurasani narrate, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, that Khawlah bint Hakim al-Sulamiyyah, and she was one of the maternal aunts of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about a woman who has a wet dream. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let her wash."
"27857","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Ibn Abi Suwayd, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, he said: The righteous woman Khawlah bint Hakim claimed that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out embracing one of the sons of his daughter, saying: By Allah, you make cowardly and miserly, and you are of the sweet fragrance of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic. And the last footing Allah trod was at Wajj. And Sufyan said once: You make miserly and you make cowardly."
"27858","Abdillah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Khawlah bint Hakim, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, you have a basin? He said: Yes, and the most beloved of those who come to me at it are your people."
"27859","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Yuhannas, that Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, when he came to Madinah, married Khawlah bint Qays ibn Qahd al-Ansariyyah of Banu al-Najjar. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to visit Hamzah in her house, and she used to narrate to him from him, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrations. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us one day, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, it has reached me from you that you narrate that you will have on the Day of Resurrection a basin from such-and-such to such-and-such. He said: Yes, and the most beloved of people to me to drink from it are your people. She said: So I brought to him a pot in which was bread or porridge, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, put his hand in the pot to eat, and his fingers were burned, so he said: Hiss. Then Ibn Adam said: If cold befalls him he says: Hiss, and if heat befalls him he says: Hiss."
"27860","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari informed us that Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah informed him that he heard Ubayd Sanuta narrate that he heard Khawlah bint Qays, and he said Khawlah al-Ansariyyah who was with Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, narrate that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon Hamzah in his house, and they were discussing the world. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The world is green and sweet. Whoever takes it rightfully is blessed in it. And many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger will have the Fire on the day he meets Allah."
